# TradeFlock USA — Editorial Design System

TradeFlock USA is a U.S. business publication in the tradition of IBTimes:
a clean white canvas, hairline rules, dense multi-column news pages, and
serif headlines that read as journalism — not as a SaaS marketing site.

Prefer Next.js App Router Server Components. Fetch on the server. Keep
client components small and only for interaction (mobile menu, ticker
pause). Do not introduce a global client wrapper.

## Color & surface

- Page background is always `bg-white`. Body text is near-black (`text-neutral-900`).
- Do not use dark mode, zinc/slate page backgrounds, gradients, or glassmorphism.
- Hairline borders only: `border-neutral-200` (1px). No thick rules except the
  masthead underline (`border-b` / `border-t`) and the category bar.
- Accent is spare: a single newsroom red (`#c41e3a`) for BREAKING, kicker labels,
  and "Most Read" numerals. Links hover to this red; they are otherwise inherited.
- Do not use drop shadows, `rounded-xl` cards, or colored section backgrounds.
  Thumbnails may be `rounded-none`.

## Typography

- Display / headlines: Playfair Display (`font-serif`). Tight tracking on the
  masthead; slightly tight tracking on story headlines (`tracking-tight`).
- UI, kickers, bylines, body: Source Sans 3 (`font-sans`).
- Kickers (section labels) are 11–12px, uppercase, letterspaced (`tracking-widest`),
  `font-semibold`, often red or `text-neutral-500`.
- Headlines scale down quickly. Homepage hero can be `text-3xl`–`text-5xl`;
  secondary cards `text-lg`–`text-xl`; rails and lists `text-sm`–`text-base`.
- Body copy on article pages uses `@tailwindcss/typography` (`prose prose-neutral`)
  with a readable measure (`max-w-3xl`), not full-bleed paragraphs.
- Datelines and timestamps use tabular, compact sans (`text-xs text-neutral-500`).

## Layout density

- Desktop homepages are a 3-column asymmetric grid: a wide hero, a stacked
  secondary column of thumbnail + headline cards, and a narrow right rail
  for numbered Most Read (1–5).
- Gutters are tight: `gap-4` / `gap-6` and `px-4` / `max-w-[1240px]`.
- Stack columns below `lg`. Do not hide the Most Read rail on tablet if it
  can wrap below the hero.
- Article pages: reading column + right rail of related stories, divided by
  a hairline (`border-l border-neutral-200`).
- Prefer dividing lines between stacked items (`divide-y divide-neutral-200`)
  over cards-in-a-card.

## Components & data

- `Header` includes: breaking ticker, New York dateline, wordmark, category nav.
- Categories are Tech, Markets, Leadership, Finance. Do not invent a consumer
  tabloid taxonomy.
- Read from Supabase in Server Components via `src/lib/supabase/server.ts`.
  Fall back to `src/lib/data/seed.ts` when env vars are missing so the UI
  remains populated in local/dev builds.
- Dynamic article routes live at `/news/[slug]` and must export
  `generateMetadata` (title, description, Open Graph).
- Images: `next/image` with explicit `sizes`. Remote hosts must be allowlisted
  in `next.config.ts`.

## Code defaults

- TypeScript strict. No `any`.
- Use the `cn()` helper (`clsx` + `tailwind-merge`) for conditional classes.
- Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only when hooks or
  browser APIs are required.
- Do not add authentication UI, dashboards, or CRUD unless explicitly asked.
  This is a reader-facing publication.
